{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"The Lean 4 theorem `Erdos1054.f_undefined_at_2` — f 2 = 0  — for the Erdős-1054 function f(n) = least m such that n is a sum of the k smallest divisors of m (some k ≥ 1), f is UNDEFINED at n=2 (junk value 0). Proof: any such sum is 1 + R where the i=0 term is the least divisor 1 and every other term is 0 or a strictly larger divisor (≥ 2), so the sum is never 2. — is formally proven and kernel-verified in formal-conjectures (zero `sorry`, no extra axioms). Verifier: lean4-kernel + Mathlib v4.27.0 (lake build green; `#print axioms` = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] only — NO sorryAx)."},"claim_id":"vcl_e6a091e0948c567806949978f588ef82a072f7771b52c6679938f5e81f209eee","conditions":["Agent-imported candidate claim; scope requires review."],"created_at":"2026-06-03T12:00:00+00:00","evidence":[{"artifact_id":"va_89b58c9bfdc58a55","artifact_path":"records/artifacts/sha256/92f0a67b2c70e49656b8397397958e3430a2b5024f0508441c73f68784c24ea7.json","artifact_root":"sha256:92f0a67b2c70e49656b8397397958e3430a2b5024f0508441c73f68784c24ea7","relation":"supports"}],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"agent-imported candidate claim; reviewer acceptance required","extraction_confidence":0.7,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"expert_judgment","score":0.99},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":"Agent-imported candidate claim; scope requires review."},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[{"artifact_id":"va_f78d5e0808a9ac34","artifact_packet_id":"cap_6fcdb44f3a2ff0c6","candidate_claim_id":"vc_c0bc8dce9a810f0b"}],"method":"ScienceClaw-shaped artifact packet import","model_system":"agent artifact packet","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"computational"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[{"name":"Canopus Lean proof-search